{
  "_comment": [
    "Foreign names the Serbian pipeline pushed through a Latin/Cyrillic round trip.",
    "'Walt Whitman' was transliterated letter by letter into Cyrillic and brought",
    "back, so w became v, y became i, x became k and qu became ku: 'Valt Vhitman'.",
    "The left-hand side is what the pack says today; the right-hand side is the",
    "form Serbian actually uses, taken from the transcription the explanations",
    "around each option already write ('Kjubrik', 'Bigl', 'Sverpunkt').",
    "Names Serbian keeps in their original spelling - band names, ship names,",
    "acronyms, Latin binomials, album and painting titles - are restored to it.",
    "Entries the round trip happened to land on correctly (Darvin, Atila, Magelan,",
    "Posejdon, Pompeji, Tajvan, Kuvait, Artritis, Eter, Agaton, Hezbolah) are",
    "A second, smaller group rides along: French names that reached Serbian with their accents stripped and their spelling untouched, next to the transcriptions the same pack already writes ('Pol Sezan', 'Ežen Delakroa').",
    "deliberately absent: there is nothing to repair."
  ],
